X: 1
T: Son ar Chistr
O: Traditional Breton
N: "The Song of Cider" — a Breton drinking song, most likely written by
N: Jean-Bernard and Jean-Marie Prima around 1929 in the older kan ha diskan style.
N: Note values doubled from the 2/4 source so the moving value is a quarter.
N: Transposed down a minor third from the source's C minor to A minor.
N: Melody from flutetunes.com, cross-checked against Paul de Grae's setting on
N: tunearch.org (in E minor) — the two agree note for note.
L: 1/8
Q: 1/2=136
M: 4/4
K: Am
